cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  food-nutrition: a reproducible pipeline for harmonising, imputing and
  integrating cross-national food composition databases
message: >-
  If you use this software or the dataset it produces, please cite it using the
  metadata in this file, and cite the three source databases listed in the
  README.
type: software
abstract: >-
  Python pipeline that validates, links and integrates food composition
  databases that share no common identifier. It performs FAO/INFOODS-based
  source validation, TF-IDF cosine entity resolution within category blocks,
  per-source missing-data mechanism diagnosis, hold-out evaluation with
  per-nutrient method selection, imputation including cross-database transfer
  (MissForest trained on a denser source and applied to a sparser one),
  bootstrap uncertainty quantification, and a final integration step that
  records the provenance of every cell. Applied to the Indonesian Food
  Composition Table (TKPI), the Malaysian Food Composition Database (MyFCD) and
  USDA SR Legacy.
